What changed and why:
- **`ObservableObject` and `@Published` became `@Observable`.** Views then only re-render for the properties they actually read. Use `@State` in place of `@StateObject`.
- **`DispatchQueue.global().async` and `main.async` are gone.** `await` doesn't leave the main actor, so `items` and `isLoading` are set directly on main with no hop-back code.
- **`@concurrent` on `parse` keeps the heavy work off the main thread.** This is the one place that needs to leave main. Without the attribute, an `async` function would stay on the main actor.
- **`Parser` and `Item` are `nonisolated`.** Otherwise default isolation would make them main-actor types. `Item` is `Sendable` because it's returned across isolation boundaries. Make it a value type with `Sendable` members.
- **`try! Data(contentsOf:)` became `URLSession.data(from:)`.** The old call was blocking I/O that crashed on failure. The new one is async, cancellable, and works with file URLs too. Errors land in `error`.
- **Cancellation is handled.** `.task` cancels the load when the view disappears. `parse` checks `Task.checkCancellation()` before the expensive work.
